<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head><meta charset="UTF-8" /><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" /><title>Keep your TrackGeek account</title></head>
<body style="margin:0;padding:40px 20px;background:#0e0e12;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:#ffffff;">
  <table role="presentation" style="max-width:580px;margin:auto;background:#202026;border-radius:10px;padding:32px;">
    <tr><td>
      <h1 style="font-size:26px;">Keep your TrackGeek account</h1>
      <p>Hello, {{name}}.</p>
      <p>We have not seen activity on your TrackGeek account for at least five months.</p>
      <p>Unless you return, your account and all its data will be permanently deleted on or after <strong>{{deletionDate}} (UTC)</strong>. Your library, lists, reviews, screenshots and activity cannot be recovered after deletion. Any recurring subscription will be cancelled.</p>
      <p>Sign in and use TrackGeek before that date to keep your account. If you are already signed in, open TrackGeek again using your existing session.</p>
      <p style="padding:16px 0;"><a href="{{url}}" style="background:#10b981;color:#ffffff;padding:14px 24px;border-radius:8px;text-decoration:none;">Keep my account</a></p>
      <p>Returning resets the inactivity period. No other action is needed.</p>
    </td></tr>
  </table>
</body>
</html>
